WEBVTT

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:03.400
Next is today's second match!

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:11.120
Yuya Sakaki from You Show School vs 
Shingo Sawatari from Leo Duel School!

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:13.020
Do your best!

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:14.220
Yuya!

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:15.320
Hang tough!

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:18.400
Get fired up!  Let your blood boil!

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:23.680
Yuya, this is your first battle to get 
closer to your father.  Give it your all.

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:26.480
So that's the Pendulum user.

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:30.380
But some people say that Pendulum isn't real.

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:35.440
There are rumors that his duel 
against Strong Ishijima was fake.

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:51.880
What is he cosplaying as?

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:54.800
That's "Mother's Eye" by Hasegawa.

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:57.440
The cards are calling me.

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:00.000
They're asking me to draw them.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.120
The lone star twinkling in the heavens!

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:04.510
Witness dueling's #1 star!

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:11.920
Do you know who I am?

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:13.520
Sawatari.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:14.820
Wrong!

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:19.770
I'm Neo New Sawatari!

00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:23.600
Neo New Sawatari is the best!

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:25.280
Neo New?

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:27.480
Don't they mean the same thing?

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:29.540
That was cool.

00:01:30.370 --> 00:01:36.100
Implementing mass into Solid 
Vision has created Action Duels.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:41.080
In duels where the field, monsters 
and duelists become one,

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:44.190
the people are caught in 
a frenzy of excitement!

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:48.350
Let's start!  From an instant flash

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:51.080
Let's find!  Yeah, the way I ought to go

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:53.750
Let's start!  The fun is only getting started

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:56.550
Ready go!  The real beginning

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:07.670
A future filled with hope 
and anxiety now begins

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:13.140
Don't worry because you have firm desires

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:18.740
I fight to reach the day that I yearn for

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:22.880
The gleaming strength resides inside the card

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:26.820
Repeating Up/Down

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:29.150
Feel It!  The heartbeat Bu,Bu,Bu,Burn!

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:36.430
I become stronger by overcoming 
and shaking off limitations again

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:39.860
Because I don't want to give up

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:44.870
Ride the accelerating wind and head towards

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:51.940
My dream that makes me love tomorrow

00:02:51.940 --> 00:03:02.450
Break through those clouds and draw 
your dazzling dreams in the blue sky

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:05.160
Let's start!  From an instant flash

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:07.860
Let's find!  Yeah, the way I ought to go

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:10.660
Let's start!  The fun is only getting started

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:13.430
Ready go!  The real beginning

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:22.950
Howling Whirlwind  Yosen Lost Tornado!

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:27.190
Yuya Sakaki, I have numerous 
grudges against you.

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:29.150
Grudges?

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:35.740
#1: You disgraced me by stealing 
my Pendulum Cards and defeating me!

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:38.800
But you stole those cards from me first!

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:44.450
#2: A Xyz user that looked exactly 
like you hurt and disgraced me!

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:48.170
That wasn't me, and I heard 
that you weren't actually hurt.

00:03:48.470 --> 00:03:54.330
#3: You assaulted and hurt my dear Papa!  
There's no greater disgrace than that!

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:56.360
That wasn't me.

00:03:56.930 --> 00:04:01.650
You disgraced me many times, but I'll 
now pay you back hundreds of times over!

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:03.620
I'll make this declaration:

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:09.090
Yuya Sakaki, you will suffer the greatest 
disgrace in this duel and lose.

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:13.570
Whoa!  Sawatari already declared victory!

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:16.770
He makes long introductions.

00:04:17.300 --> 00:04:20.930
Until now, Pendulum Summon 
guided you to victory.

00:04:20.930 --> 00:04:24.740
But today, it will lead you to defeat.

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:28.210
I'll lose due to Pendulum Summon?

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:37.860
It's rumored that Leo Corporation 
is developing Pendulum Cards.

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:44.360
I'll get those cards first 
and use them to defeat you.

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:48.040
Does Sawatari have Pendulum Cards?

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:51.000
What's going to happen in this match?

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:55.480
Let's select the Action Field!  C'mon!

00:04:57.600 --> 00:04:59.540
The choice is made!

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:01.810
Action Field on!

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:07.100
The Field Spell Sunset Stronghold activates!

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:24.090
Let's go!  The duelists 
meet at the battlefield!

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:26.930
Along with their monsters, they'll kick 
the ground and fly through the sky...

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:28.810
...to move around the field!

00:05:28.810 --> 00:05:33.480
Witness dueling's greatest 
evolution!  Action!

00:05:33.610 --> 00:05:34.760
Duel!

00:05:39.370 --> 00:05:41.370
I'll let you go first.

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:43.940
My turn!

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:47.520
When neither player has 
a monster on the field,

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:50.560
I can summon this card from my 
hand by lowering its Level by 1!

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:54.000
I summon Performapal Drummerilla!

00:05:56.420 --> 00:05:59.100
I set one card and end my turn.

00:05:59.350 --> 00:06:03.810
Shingo Sawatari's legendary 
revenge duel begins.

00:06:04.060 --> 00:06:06.980
My turn!  I draw!

00:06:07.250 --> 00:06:11.020
I activate the Continuous 
Spell Yosen Training Grounds!

00:06:11.020 --> 00:06:14.820
Whenever I Summon or 
Special Summon a Yosenju,

00:06:15.070 --> 00:06:19.020
one Yosen Counter lights up on this card.

00:06:19.220 --> 00:06:20.990
Yosen Counter?

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:24.960
I summon Yosenju Kama 1 from my hand!

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:30.940
When Kama 1 is successfully summoned,

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:35.610
I can summon a Yosenju from 
my hand that isn't Kama 1.

00:06:35.940 --> 00:06:38.740
Come, Yosenju Kama 2!

00:06:38.740 --> 00:06:41.770
And when Kama 2 is successfully summoned,

00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:45.680
I can summon a Yosenju from 
my hand that isn't Kama 2.

00:06:46.140 --> 00:06:48.580
Yosenju Kama 3!

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:53.860
Whoa!  Sawatari summoned three times!

00:06:55.450 --> 00:07:01.330
Pendulum Summon doesn't have a monopoly 
on summoning many monsters quickly.

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:06.490
Since I summoned three Yosenjus,

00:07:06.490 --> 00:07:11.210
due to Yosen Training Grounds's effect, 
three Yosen Counters light up.

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:13.660
It's eerie.

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:15.680
That deck might be powerful.

00:07:15.880 --> 00:07:17.680
You're incredible, Sawatari!

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:19.660
I mean, Neo New Sawatari!

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:21.390
You're the strongest!

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:23.880
Kama 1's effect activates.

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:26.680
When there's another Yosenju on the field,

00:07:26.680 --> 00:07:30.860
I can return one card on your 
field to your hand once!

00:07:31.140 --> 00:07:31.830
What?

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:37.570
Return, Drummerilla!

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:44.660
This is bad!  Yuya's field is now empty!

00:07:44.660 --> 00:07:46.750
If he's attacked...

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:48.710
Here I go!  Let's battle!

00:07:48.710 --> 00:07:51.280
Kama 1 attacks you directly!

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:53.250
Sakaki is already in a pinch!

00:07:53.250 --> 00:07:54.450
Yuya!

00:07:54.690 --> 00:07:58.190
The Continuous Trap Performapal Pinch Helper!

00:07:58.370 --> 00:08:02.760
This card activates by negating 
your monster's direct attack!

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:10.490
Then I can Special Summon one Performapal 
with 800 or fewer attack points

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:12.910
from my deck by negating its effects!

00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:16.380
I Special Summon Kaleidoscorp 
in defense position!

00:08:17.160 --> 00:08:22.370
Kaleidoscorp has more defense points 
than Kama 2 or Kama 3's attack points!

00:08:22.370 --> 00:08:24.080
So you can't attack!

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:28.050
In that case, I activate Kama 2's effect.

00:08:28.280 --> 00:08:32.520
This card can attack you directly 
by halving its attack points.

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:37.200
That means it'll fly past 
the defending monster!

00:08:40.280 --> 00:08:42.400
I won't let you get an Action Card!

00:08:42.680 --> 00:08:45.870
Let's battle!  Kama 2 attacks you directly!

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:53.460
Too bad.

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:57.310
Next, Kama 3's effect activates.

00:08:57.310 --> 00:09:01.550
When another Yosenju deals you battle damage,

00:09:01.550 --> 00:09:06.400
I can add a non-Kama 3 Yosenju 
in my deck to my hand.

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:09.760
I add Yosenju Oyam.

00:09:11.540 --> 00:09:14.700
I activate Yosen Training Grounds's effect!

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:18.480
Once per turn, by using three Yosen Counters,

00:09:18.480 --> 00:09:21.640
I can add one Yosenju 
from my deck to my hand.

00:09:22.050 --> 00:09:25.460
I add Mayosenju Daibak.

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:29.250
It won't be fun if I defeat you too easily.

00:09:29.480 --> 00:09:32.720
I set one card and end my turn.

00:09:32.980 --> 00:09:38.000
When the three Kama brothers are summoned, 
they return to my hand at the end of that turn.

00:09:40.820 --> 00:09:46.400
Due to their own effects, all his monsters 
have returned to his hand.  His field is empty.

00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:47.870
Is this a trap?

00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:53.070
Let's continue the show, 
entertainment duelist Yuya Sakaki!

00:09:53.450 --> 00:09:58.040
Sawatari is super confident 
and is goading Sakaki!

00:09:58.280 --> 00:10:02.940
Even if it's a trap, I just 
have to do my own dueling!

00:10:03.340 --> 00:10:04.020
Here I go!

00:10:04.350 --> 00:10:05.880
My turn!

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:07.950
It's here!

00:10:07.950 --> 00:10:15.680
I set the Pendulum Scale with Scale 1 
Stargazer Magician and Scale 8 Timegazer Magician!

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:32.980
Now I can summon monsters between 
Level 2 and 7 simultaneously!

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:34.060
He did it!

00:10:34.060 --> 00:10:35.450
Pendulum Summon!

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:43.890
Swing, my soul's pendulum!

00:10:44.140 --> 00:10:46.860
Draw an arc of light in the sky!

00:10:46.860 --> 00:10:48.860
Pendulum Summon!

00:10:48.860 --> 00:10:50.940
Come out, my monsters!

00:10:53.020 --> 00:10:55.540
Performapal Drummerilla!

00:10:56.040 --> 00:11:00.860
And with different-colored shining 
eyes, Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:11:03.440 --> 00:11:04.580
There it is!

00:11:04.580 --> 00:11:09.520
Sakaki's Pendulum Summon that 
even defeated Strong Ishijima!

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:11.440
So this is Pendulum Summon!

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:12.990
It's real!

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:15.240
Now it's my time!

00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:20.660
When Odd-Eyes and Drummerilla 
attack directly, Yuya wins!

00:11:20.980 --> 00:11:23.580
But it totally looks like a trap.

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:28.040
Here I go!  Let's battle!

00:11:28.420 --> 00:11:31.640
Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon 
attacks you directly!

00:11:34.400 --> 00:11:37.780
Yosenju Oyam's effect activates from my hand!

00:11:37.780 --> 00:11:39.740
When I take a direct attack,

00:11:39.740 --> 00:11:42.350
I can send one Yosenju in 
my hand to the graveyard

00:11:42.350 --> 00:11:45.280
to Special Summon it in attack position!

00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:47.970
Unknown attack points?

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:50.240
Oyam's attack points become the same

00:11:50.240 --> 00:11:54.590
as the original attack points of 
the monster it's battling against!

00:11:55.920 --> 00:12:00.940
Since I Special Summoned a Yosenju, 
one Yosen Counter lights up.

00:12:01.680 --> 00:12:05.200
Well?  Will you attack knowing 
that they'll both be destroyed?

00:12:05.420 --> 00:12:08.670
I'm not done!  Drummerilla's 
effect activates!

00:12:09.360 --> 00:12:15.860
Once during battle, this card increases 
my monster's attack points by 600.

00:12:17.580 --> 00:12:19.260
Go, Odd-Eyes!

00:12:19.260 --> 00:12:21.390
Spiral Strike Burst!

00:12:23.420 --> 00:12:28.090
When the destroyed monster is Level 
5-or-above, battle damage is doubled!

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:36.780
That hurt!  Sawatari took 
1200 points of damage!

00:12:37.180 --> 00:12:39.100
Oyam's effect activates!

00:12:39.420 --> 00:12:46.580
When this card is destroyed in battle, 
I can add one Oyam to my hand!

00:12:46.800 --> 00:12:52.050
Whoa!  Just when Yuya managed to destroy 
Oyam, he adds a new one to his hand!

00:12:52.300 --> 00:12:55.860
Even if I attack now, 
Oyam will come out again.

00:12:55.860 --> 00:12:57.320
I'll wait for now.

00:12:57.710 --> 00:12:59.620
I end my turn!

00:13:02.240 --> 00:13:07.000
This is only the start of Shingo 
Sawatari's legendary revenge duel.

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:12.000
Yuya Sakaki, you will learn how 
terrifying Pendulum Summon is!

00:13:13.400 --> 00:13:16.180
How terrifying Pendulum Summon is?

00:13:16.340 --> 00:13:19.650
Sheesh, he just keeps talking and talking.

00:13:19.860 --> 00:13:22.380
Watch, Yuya Sakaki!

00:13:22.880 --> 00:13:24.150
My turn!

00:13:25.860 --> 00:13:28.480
I summon Yosenju Kama 1!

00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:37.280
By summoning Kama 1, I can 
summon Kama 2 and Kama 3!

00:13:38.220 --> 00:13:41.620
Yosen Training Grounds's effect activates!

00:13:41.620 --> 00:13:46.670
Since I summoned three Yosenjus, 
three Yosen Counters light up.

00:13:46.670 --> 00:13:51.880
Sawatari has once again instantly 
summoned three monsters on his field!

00:13:52.100 --> 00:13:55.500
This is the same as Sawatari's last turn!

00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:59.850
If nothing changes, Kama 1's effect 
will send Odd-Eyes back to his hand!

00:14:00.010 --> 00:14:01.320
Let's battle!

00:14:01.620 --> 00:14:06.290
Due to Kama 2's effect, it can attack you 
directly by halving its attack points!

00:14:06.510 --> 00:14:07.930
A direct attack?

00:14:08.260 --> 00:14:11.100
What?  He won't use Kama 1's effect?

00:14:12.140 --> 00:14:13.470
Something must be up.

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:24.280
Yuya!

00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:27.020
Kama 3's effect activates!

00:14:27.020 --> 00:14:34.220
When another Yosenju deals you damage, 
I add one Yosenju to my hand.

00:14:34.440 --> 00:14:39.370
I add the Pendulum Monster Yosenju Shinchu L!

00:14:40.420 --> 00:14:43.660
Whoa!  Sawatari has a Pendulum Card!

00:14:44.660 --> 00:14:46.630
So you really do have one.

00:14:46.840 --> 00:14:48.520
Pendulum Monster?

00:14:48.520 --> 00:14:49.600
No way!

00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:53.920
Yosen Training Grounds's effect activates!

00:14:53.920 --> 00:14:59.480
By using three Yosen Counters, I can add 
one Yosenju from my deck to my hand.

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:05.450
I add the Pendulum Monster 
Yosenju Shinchu R to my hand!

00:15:05.680 --> 00:15:08.190
Two Pendulum Cards.

00:15:08.190 --> 00:15:13.940
Yuya Sakaki, just like I said, Pendulum 
Summon will lead you to defeat!

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:22.910
I set the Pendulum Scale with Scale 3 
Yosenju Shinchu L and Scale 5 Yosenju Shinchu R!

00:15:34.350 --> 00:15:35.520
It's coming.

00:15:35.520 --> 00:15:40.000
But since it's Scale 3 and 5, you 
can only summon Level 4 monsters.

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:41.970
Level 4?

00:15:42.620 --> 00:15:44.320
Too bad.

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:47.650
Yosenju Shinchu R's effect activates!

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:51.790
When there's a Yosenju in 
the other Pendulum Zone,

00:15:51.790 --> 00:15:54.830
the Pendulum Scale rises to 11!

00:15:56.220 --> 00:16:00.100
Now I can summon monsters between 
Level 4 and 10 simultaneously!

00:16:00.100 --> 00:16:01.860
Pendulum Summon!

00:16:03.280 --> 00:16:06.370
The elder ghost clad in strong winds,

00:16:06.370 --> 00:16:11.120
remove your wild garments to create a 
large river and hollow out the land!

00:16:11.620 --> 00:16:15.620
Come out, Mayosenju Daibak!

00:16:31.240 --> 00:16:35.640
I'm surprised!  Sawatari Pendulum Summoned!

00:16:36.180 --> 00:16:40.050
Pendulum energy detected.  
Physical image level normal.

00:16:40.780 --> 00:16:43.570
Power balance and output are both stable.

00:16:43.570 --> 00:16:45.820
President, you've succeeded!

00:16:49.300 --> 00:16:51.720
Neo New Sawatari is amazing!

00:16:51.720 --> 00:16:53.730
Yosenjus are the mightiest!

00:16:54.140 --> 00:16:57.430
One Yosen Counter lights up 
on Yosen Training Grounds.

00:16:57.780 --> 00:17:01.600
Isn't Yuya Sakaki the only 
one who can Pendulum?

00:17:01.600 --> 00:17:04.170
But Sawatari just used it 
right before your eyes!

00:17:04.510 --> 00:17:06.700
I knew this day would come,

00:17:06.700 --> 00:17:09.880
but I didn't think someone 
would Pendulum Summon so early.

00:17:10.080 --> 00:17:13.350
And the monster he summoned is Level 10!

00:17:13.350 --> 00:17:16.020
That's right!  Get excited!  
Get more excited!

00:17:16.020 --> 00:17:17.870
The fun is only getting started!

00:17:18.100 --> 00:17:20.320
That's Yuya's catchphrase!

00:17:20.740 --> 00:17:25.290
I'm the chosen one.  Neo New Sawatari!

00:17:25.650 --> 00:17:29.960
And I'm not just able to Pendulum Summon!

00:17:29.960 --> 00:17:31.310
I'll go beyond that!

00:17:31.540 --> 00:17:32.760
Beyond that?

00:17:32.980 --> 00:17:34.770
I activate Daibak's effect!

00:17:35.180 --> 00:17:39.040
When this card is successfully summoned,

00:17:39.040 --> 00:17:43.010
I select two cards on the field 
and return them to the hand!

00:17:43.180 --> 00:17:47.980
I return Stargazer Magician and 
Timegazer Magician to your hand!

00:17:49.650 --> 00:17:50.970
I'm not done!

00:17:50.970 --> 00:17:52.990
Since Daibak is on the field,

00:17:52.990 --> 00:17:56.990
I activate the Continuous Trap 
Dizzying Winds of Yosen Village!

00:17:58.720 --> 00:18:01.950
When non-Yosenju cards return 
from your field to your hand,

00:18:01.950 --> 00:18:04.660
they return to your deck instead!

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:08.130
Pendulum Cards return to the deck?

00:18:08.130 --> 00:18:11.600
Sakaki can't Pendulum Summon!

00:18:11.860 --> 00:18:19.020
I pay 800 life points to activate the 
Continuous Spell Yosen Whirlwind from my hand!

00:18:19.680 --> 00:18:21.080
I end my turn.

00:18:22.050 --> 00:18:24.800
But it's not a normal end of the turn.

00:18:24.800 --> 00:18:29.790
I'll show you Sawatari's legendary 
combo: Yosen Lost Tornado!

00:18:30.310 --> 00:18:32.260
Yosen Lost Tornado?

00:18:32.540 --> 00:18:38.240
When a Yosenju on my 
field returns to my hand,

00:18:38.240 --> 00:18:41.730
Yosen Whirlwind returns one card 
on your field to your hand.

00:18:41.830 --> 00:18:44.960
And when a non-Yosenju 
card returns to the hand,

00:18:44.960 --> 00:18:49.940
Dizzying Winds of Yosen Village returns 
it to the deck instead of the hand.

00:18:51.320 --> 00:18:54.910
The three Kama brothers return 
to my hand during the End Phase.

00:18:55.120 --> 00:19:00.120
Therefore, Yosen Whirlwind returns 
three cards to your hand,

00:19:00.120 --> 00:19:02.820
but Dizzying Winds return 
them to your deck instead!

00:19:03.560 --> 00:19:08.820
Return, Pinch Helper, 
Kaleidoscorp and Drummerilla!

00:19:09.480 --> 00:19:12.840
Cards are leaving Yuya's field!

00:19:12.840 --> 00:19:14.500
Only Odd-Eyes is left!

00:19:15.870 --> 00:19:18.470
I'll make sure it leaves too!

00:19:18.960 --> 00:19:20.940
Daibak's effect activates!

00:19:21.140 --> 00:19:25.620
When it's Special Summoned, it returns 
to my hand at the end of the turn.

00:19:26.260 --> 00:19:28.880
Yosen Lost Tornado!

00:19:32.560 --> 00:19:35.050
Bye bye, Odd-Eyes.

00:19:35.260 --> 00:19:36.530
I see!

00:19:36.530 --> 00:19:40.030
That's why he didn't use Kama 1's 
effect at the start of this turn.

00:19:40.030 --> 00:19:44.940
His goal was to return Odd-Eyes 
to my deck instead of my hand.

00:19:45.720 --> 00:19:46.700
How's that?

00:19:46.700 --> 00:19:49.960
Just like their names, Yosen 
Whirlwind whirls up your cards,

00:19:49.960 --> 00:19:54.490
and Dizzying Winds sends those 
dazed cards to your deck.

00:19:55.080 --> 00:20:00.450
This is Sawatari's legendary 
combo Yosen Lost Tornado!

00:20:00.920 --> 00:20:03.840
He sealed away Yuya Sakaki's Pendulum.

00:20:03.840 --> 00:20:06.380
That's well done for Sawatari.

00:20:06.380 --> 00:20:09.420
But his name for the combo is the worst.

00:20:09.640 --> 00:20:14.420
I am Neo New Sawatari, the 
man who has created a legend.

00:20:15.800 --> 00:20:20.160
Finally, Shinchu R's Pendulum 
Scale returns to normal.

00:20:20.980 --> 00:20:24.400
President, this is your idea 
of how to stop Pendulum.

00:20:24.700 --> 00:20:29.000
Even if you return Pendulum 
to the hand or destroy it,

00:20:29.000 --> 00:20:31.210
it can resurrect on the next turn.

00:20:31.210 --> 00:20:33.460
That is its greatest strength.

00:20:33.460 --> 00:20:36.500
But if you can return it to the deck...

00:20:37.660 --> 00:20:40.320
Sakaki's field is empty!

00:20:40.320 --> 00:20:43.920
He only has one card in his hand, 
so he's in a desperate situation!

00:20:44.430 --> 00:20:47.520
You're finished on my next turn.

00:20:47.520 --> 00:20:49.900
Let's see your final pointless move.

00:20:50.120 --> 00:20:52.700
If he can't use Pendulum...

00:20:52.700 --> 00:20:55.100
What's going to happen to Yuya?

00:20:55.840 --> 00:20:57.340
My turn.

00:20:57.560 --> 00:21:00.460
Yuya, don't give up!  Get fired up!

00:21:00.460 --> 00:21:01.920
Show that you're a man!

00:21:01.920 --> 00:21:03.310
Yuya!

00:21:03.730 --> 00:21:04.580
Wait!

00:21:07.060 --> 00:21:09.260
Yuya is smiling.

00:21:09.260 --> 00:21:09.950
What?

00:21:10.330 --> 00:21:13.330
I am completely cornered.

00:21:13.560 --> 00:21:14.660
However...

00:21:15.660 --> 00:21:17.160
I wonder why...

00:21:18.230 --> 00:21:21.530
I'm really excited right now!

00:21:22.080 --> 00:21:25.100
I'll finish our fight!

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:27.830
Finish?  Don't be silly.

00:21:28.040 --> 00:21:30.070
The duel has only just begun!

00:21:30.260 --> 00:21:31.580
What?

00:21:31.800 --> 00:21:33.140
I draw!

00:21:33.140 --> 00:21:36.900
I set two cards and end my turn!

00:21:37.860 --> 00:21:39.280
What?  That's it?

00:21:39.280 --> 00:21:44.750
C'mon!  I thought things were about to 
get exciting, but that was very basic.

00:21:45.040 --> 00:21:47.710
Well, I guess you can't do anything 
because you can't Pendulum Summon

00:21:47.710 --> 00:21:50.260
and have no cards in your hand.

00:21:51.030 --> 00:21:54.660
If I don't have any cards, I 
just have to search for them!

00:21:54.960 --> 00:21:55.900
Huh?

00:21:58.180 --> 00:21:59.280
Yuya!

00:21:59.280 --> 00:22:00.620
He's fine.

00:22:01.040 --> 00:22:03.800
His eyes are still strong and alive.

00:22:08.240 --> 00:22:10.900
The fun is only getting started!

00:22:31.250 --> 00:22:35.860
As long as there's a smile

00:22:38.120 --> 00:22:42.630
I'll risk my ultimate pride

00:22:45.090 --> 00:22:47.940
I always believe

00:22:48.130 --> 00:22:51.480
In my tomorrow

00:22:51.830 --> 00:22:57.080
With courageous wings
Just fly away!

00:23:00.380 --> 00:23:05.720
This duel of the soul 
(Break through the darkness with the miracle card!)

00:23:05.720 --> 00:23:12.600
A battle that surpasses clashing dimensions 
(The fun is only getting started!)

00:23:12.790 --> 00:23:19.270
For everyone to acquire their own dreams

00:23:19.830 --> 00:23:23.340
We go towards the mightiest future

00:23:49.170 --> 00:23:52.040
How pathetic, Yuya Sakaki.

00:23:52.040 --> 00:23:55.800
You're afraid of my 
magnificent Pendulum Summon.

00:23:55.800 --> 00:23:59.360
But I'll finish you on my next turn!

00:23:59.370 --> 00:24:03.560
Your defeat will be the main event!

00:24:03.690 --> 00:24:06.650
Sorry, but I don't intend to lose either!

00:24:06.650 --> 00:24:08.930
I'll show you the greatest show!

00:24:08.990 --> 00:24:13.860
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V:
Fierce Battle!  Entertainment Duel Show!!

00:24:13.860 --> 00:24:16.520
The fun is only getting started!
